From 8532cf9fb1187d321fad2290009ff14b9a90787d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:13:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx179: retain state after failed stream stop

The LTS driver already has the sensor tables, controls and power
sequence. Retain its runtime PM reference when the standby write
fails, matching the V4L2 core stream state so retry cannot drop a
reference twice. Reject ACTIVE format changes while streaming and
preserve TRY negotiation. Keep the LTS callback signatures and every
other driver byte. Add the driver to its proposed maintainer entry.
The source-extracted sensor/core models reproduce nine failures across
378 cases before repair and none afterward.

The complete camera set builds 78 native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT
objects without W=1 diagnostics or permissive CFI. Source checksums
match ELF line tables. Three source-only CAMSS partial links retain no
unresolved MIPI timing helper; these are not final Kbuild module or
kernel links. Low-level hardware, locks, full PM/driver core and
capture are modeled or untested. Physical acceptance and the r2
display fault remain open.

Original proposals are by Timothy Schmidt with Claude Opus 5.5
assistance; Codex (GPT-6) prepared this maintained-LTS reconciliation
and qualification. Original author/date and all source/license notices
are preserved. Human DCO and review remain pending; no sign-off, phone
action or publication is claimed.

Backported from commit ad5ba0e48070 ("media: i2c: Add Sony IMX179
sensor support")
---
 MAINTAINERS                | 1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MAINTAINERS b/MAINTAINERS
index 4f21ab9a11fb4..a5b9527274401 100644
--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -23956,6 +23956,7 @@ M:	Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
 L:	linux-media@vger.kernel.org
 S:	Maintained
 F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/sony,imx179.yaml
+F:	drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c
 
 SONY IMX208 SENSOR DRIVER
 M:	Sakari Ailus <sakari.ailus@linux.intel.com>
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c
index 6c1bd72e28f55..7cbe81d619202 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c
@@ -362,6 +362,10 @@ static int imx179_set_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	const struct imx179_mode *mode;
 	int vblank, ret;
 
+	if (fmt->which == V4L2_SUBDEV_FORMAT_ACTIVE &&
+	    v4l2_subdev_is_streaming(sd))
+		return -EBUSY;
+
 	mode = v4l2_find_nearest_size(imx179_modes, ARRAY_SIZE(imx179_modes),
 				      width, height, fmt->format.width,
 				      fmt->format.height);
@@ -433,6 +437,9 @@ static int imx179_disable_streams(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 
 	ret = cci_write(imx179->regmap, IMX179_REG_MODE_SELECT,
 			IMX179_MODE_STANDBY, NULL);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	pm_runtime_put(imx179->dev);
 
 	return ret;
-- 
